IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtva-licensing`
IMPORT `rtva-qa`

-- Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (rtva-qa.l4): every exported question, for every
-- role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation. Each question that
-- takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does not hold and every
-- input after it ASSUMEd. For the baseline's seat (the owner, the seller and the buyer) the answers are also asserted
-- equal to the baseline's own export on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text (the
-- quotations in rtva-licensing.l4): PU $50; r 57 $13.20 + $29.76 per 100 kg or part, at most $586; 15 days' grace.
-- Chloe's used car (c074): tare 1 400 kg, GVM 1 900 kg, duty $770, CTP premium $450 (HYPOTHETICAL figures, as in the
-- baseline's cases).
--
-- Generated by gen_rtva.py in the session scratchpad. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked kind of vehicle` IS A `Kind of vehicle`
ASSUME `an unasked licence state` IS A `Licence status`
ASSUME `an unasked period` IS A `Licence period`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own a vehicle`
`as the seller` MEANS `I am selling, or have sold, a licensed vehicle`
`as the buyer` MEANS `I am buying, or have bought, a licensed vehicle`
`as the user` MEANS `I drive or ride a vehicle that is not mine`

